<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-emiliania-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Emiliania huxleyi Holocene Turing wavelength at 5.808 nm (pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 82.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg kinetics with the Turing peak fixed at 5.808 nm (0 Ma, extant). Selection-band Pearson r = 0.994, RMSE = 0.018. The first coccolith annulus used raw intensity and was a poor spoke estimator (spoke score 0.22, harmonic 40, centre on the panel edge). The damped wing was not yet reported separately. Those two items are the remediation list. The SEM is micrometre-scale; the field is 5.808 nm. Overall 82.7/100 (faithfulness 81.1, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/emiliania_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-emiliania-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 3694038 B, 720×540 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 c90f6524d06e8f07e81b20c7b2d4f9eee909c6aa048c4f0038497905019d3692 (sha256 c90f6524d06e8f07e81b20c7b2d4f9eee909c6aa048c4f0038497905019d3692), spec_fingerprint ccb36351ddf24d5f1022c17c85f5291551afc2f963515079e7b0ebff6253d163. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ccb36351ddf24d5f1022c17c85f5291551afc2f963515079e7b0ebff6253d163; artifact_sha256: c90f6524d06e8f07e81b20c7b2d4f9eee909c6aa048c4f0038497905019d3692; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/emiliania_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/emiliania_huxleyi_coccosphere_coccolith.jpg=94d4b431c4912727..., datasets/emiliania_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/emiliania_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=7eca0ef524dbb598...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavelength from reaction and diffusion. | Schnakenberg 1979 gives f = a - u + u^2 v and g = b - u^2 v. | Henriksen et al. 2004: Emiliania CAP blocks acute calcite steps. Young & Henriksen 2003: coccolith calcite grows inside a vesicle.; reconstructed_in_script: a, b and the diffusion ratio are set so lambda_c is exactly 5.808 nm. | The predecessor spacing 7.744 nm is six modes on the eight-mode Holocene patch.; transfer_boundary: The CC BY-SA SEM is a micrometre-scale coccosphere and coccolith. The GIF maps the molecular activator onto that geometry.; does_not_claim: That Emiliania forms pigment stripes or ocelli at 5.8 nm. | That 7.744 nm was measured on a fossil. | That CAP kinetics are Schnakenberg kinetics.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=1.9]: Tangential-Sobel spoke count on the real coccolith.",
        "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=1.3]: Separate damped-wing RMSE at a smaller dt.",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Replace the raw-intensity coccolith annulus (spoke score 0.22, harmonic 40) with a tangential-Sobel annulus so the spoke count is actually measured on the SEM.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Report the damped-wing growth-rate RMSE separately and integrate that wing at a smaller timestep than the selection band.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.27e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-emiliania-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
